{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-85c9679b-c5ef-4e69-857a-8a6d7f44cd16","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-99527986132d6d52","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-oj_aquik/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001.md","content":"# Expose per-project Kueue GPU quota data for administrator consumption reporting\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers a consumable, per-project view of Kueue GPU quota and\ncurrent quota usage in the Distributed Workloads component, so that\nadministrator-facing chargeback reporting can compare each project's GPU-hour\nconsumption against its Kueue quota. Today the platform's Kueue metrics\nexpose pending/admitted workload counts per queue, which is not sufficient\nfor per-project GPU quota comparison; this epic provides that data surface.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Expose, per project (namespace), the project's Kueue GPU quota and current\n  quota usage, derived from the platform's Kueue quota model\n  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue semantics).\n- Choose and implement the exposure surface (metrics, custom resource, or\n  API) — an implementation decision for the Distributed Workloads team; the\n  strategy does not prescribe one.\n- Document the exposed data contract (shape and semantics of the per-project\n  quota information) for consuming teams.\n- Ensure projects without a Kueue quota are represented predictably\n  (reportable as no-quota) rather than omitted silently.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- For every project that has a Kueue GPU quota, the project's GPU quota and\n  current quota usage are retrievable through the exposed surface.\n- The exposed quota information is consistent with the platform's Kueue\n  quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue semantics), verified against the\n  deployed Kueue configuration.\n- The data contract of the exposed surface is documented.\n- Existing Kueue queueing and admission behavior is unchanged (regression\n  check on the queueing path).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1) — enables the quota side of \"current-month consumption against\n  each project's Kueue quota\" in the administrator view.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":54248,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-913a72913d7c060a","agent_id":"a7ae081040d55e322","session_id":"bb15c9ed-6003-4c9d-b6c4-e899274a0ed5","uuid":"93777210-ff19-4fe5-bff8-a58d9ada218d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:37:02.481Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
