{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ff2d54a7-0e2b-4b60-bd05-cfd50af1496f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b511d593413ab92b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-oj_aquik/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports with CSV export and reporting API\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the administrator-facing per-project GPU-hour consumption\nreporting in the Dashboard: reports of per-project GPU-hour usage over\nselectable time ranges, computed from the per-project GPU-hour usage data\ndelivered by the GPU usage metering work (RHAISTRAT-9990). It also delivers\nthe export and retrieval access modes of the same reports — CSV export and a\nstable API for finance tooling. Collection of usage data is owned by the\nmetering strategy and is not re-implemented here.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Administrator report view in the Dashboard: per-project GPU-hour\n  consumption over administrator-selectable time ranges.\n- Report computation consumes the metering data as delivered by the GPU\n  usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990); no re-implementation of usage\n  collection.\n- CSV export of the displayed report (same project/time-range data).\n- Stable retrieval API over the same report data, suitable for finance\n  tooling integration.\n- Administrator-only access to the reports, export, and API.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- An administrator can view per-project GPU-hour consumption for a\n  selectable time range, computed from the delivered metering data.\n- The report for a given project and time range can be exported as CSV and\n  opens correctly in spreadsheet tooling.\n- The same report data is retrievable through a stable API usable by\n  finance tooling.\n- Report access (view, export, API) is restricted to platform\n  administrators.\n- Report computation conforms to the metering data schema as finalized by\n  the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990); schema finalization\n  changes are absorbed in the consumption layer and the reports re-validate\n  cleanly against the finalized schema.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The metering data schema is owned by RHAISTRAT-9990 and is not final until\n  that strategy lands; this epic carries that external timing risk. Reports\n  are implemented and validated against the metering data as currently\n  delivered and re-validated at finalization (fix-and-adapt).\n- The Dashboard architecture (no data plane; Kubernetes API only) does not\n  currently define a surface for non-CR time-series data or an external\n  report API; the consumption path and API surface must align with what the\n  metering strategy delivers. Flagged in the decomposition health warnings —\n  not an acceptance criterion on this epic's deliverable.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0) — administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption\n  reports over selectable time ranges.\n- HLR-2 (P1, bundled) — CSV export and stable API retrieval are access modes\n  of the same report surface built for HLR-1; they share the report data\n  structure and are not separately schedulable, so they are kept in this\n  epic rather than split out.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":54864,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-913a72913d7c060a","agent_id":"a7ae081040d55e322","session_id":"bb15c9ed-6003-4c9d-b6c4-e899274a0ed5","uuid":"2dfa7dd0-4848-44a6-a3c0-71d31be71716","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:37:15.152Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
