{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96c82569cca3d1ac","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9018 (GPU chargeback reporting for platform administrators)\n11\t\n12\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Major.\n13\t\n14\t## Strategy Parsing Notes\n15\t\n16\tThe strategy is deliberately sparse. The following required sections are\n17\tmissing or degenerate (health warnings recorded below):\n18\t\n19\t- **Affected Components** lists component names only — no \"what changes\" and\n20\t  no owner team per component. Scopes and teams were inferred (see Health\n21\t  Warnings).\n22\t- **Impacted Teams table**: absent. Teams inferred from\n23\t  `.context/architecture-context/` owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard;\n24\t  Distributed Workloads → Distributed Workloads).\n25\t- **Dependencies table**: absent. The only dependency is the frontmatter\n26\t  `depends-on: RHAISTRAT-9990` link and the Open Questions entry.\n27\t- **Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then)**: absent. Epic ACs were derived\n28\t  from the HLRs.\n29\t- **Non-Functional Requirements**: absent.\n30\t- **Staff Engineer Input**: absent — no overrides to apply.\n31\t\n32\t## Step 0 Triage\n33\t\n34\tNot below threshold: the strategy affects two components (Dashboard,\n35\tDistributed Workloads) owned by two teams, and the reporting work carries an\n36\tunresolved external data-contract dependency, so ≥67% High AI implementability\n37\tdoes not hold. Not documentation-only: HLR-1..3 require code changes. Full\n38\tdecomposition follows.\n39\t\n40\t## Open Question Evaluation (Step 3)\n41\t\n42\tThe strategy's single open question — the metering data schema finalizes only\n43\twhen RHAISTRAT-9990 lands — was evaluated against the Step 3 decision rule\n44\t(\"does the answer change which downstream epics exist or what they do?\"):\n45\t\n46\t- **Which epics exist**: unchanged. The reporting view, export/API, quota\n47\t  comparison view, and documentation epics exist regardless of the schema's\n48\t  final shape.\n49\t- **What they do**: unchanged at the functional level. The schema shape is a\n50\t  consumption-layer detail of the reporting implementation; resolution\n51\t  requires no technical work by these teams — the answer arrives when the\n52\t  sibling strategy lands. Failure mode is fix-and-adapt (adjust the\n53\t  consumption layer), i.e. an acceptance-criterion gate, not an\n54\t  investigation.\n55\t- The dependency is a sibling **internal strategy** that resolves itself\n56\t  (analogous to Rule 21's \"third party resolves\" case): modeled as a\n57\t  **precondition with tiered delivery** (see Tiered Delivery), with no epic\n58\t  invented for RHAISTRAT-9990 and no DAG edge to it (there is no epic to edge\n59\t  to).\n60\t\n61\tConclusion: **no Investigation epic**. The risk is carried as ACs plus\n62\tRisks/Notes on the consuming epics and as a health warning below.\n63\t\n64\t## Epic List\n65\t\n66\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n67\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n68\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E001 | Expose per-project Kueue GPU quota data for administrator consumption reporting | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n69\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 | Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports with CSV export and reporting API | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P0 |\n70\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Administrator view of current-month consumption against Kueue quota | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n71\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 | Documentation of chargeback report semantics and export integration | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | Documentation | P1 |\n72\t\n73\tPriorities: E002 carries HLR-1 (P0). E001 and E003 carry HLR-3 (P1). E004 is a\n74\t`docs-authoring` epic — exempt from priority inheritance; its priority is\n75\tderived from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 (HLR-4 is P2 in\n76\tthe HLR table, but the docs-authoring priority exception governs the epic).\n77\t\n78\t## Dependency DAG\n79\t\n80\t```mermaid\n81\tgraph TD\n82\t    E001[\"E001 — per-project Kueue GPU quota data (DW)\"] --> E003[\"E003 — consumption vs quota admin view\"]\n83\t    E002[\"E002 — consumption reports + CSV/API (Dashboard)\"] --> E003\n84\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 — report semantics & export docs\"]\n85\t    E002 --> E004\n86\t    E003 --> E004\n87\t```\n88\t\n89\tCritical path: E001 → E003 → E004 (and E002 → E003 → E004), length 3.\n90\t\n91\t## DAG Justification\n92\t\n93\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n94\t|------|------|-----------|\n95\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (build-against artifact) | The quota-comparison view's code builds against the per-project quota surface E001 exposes (an API/CR/metrics surface, not a configuration reference). |\n96\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 12/13 + shared-surface rule | The quota view displays current-month consumption, which is the report capability over a fixed time range; the edge prevents two epics building the same consumption-data surface independently. |\n97\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built, including the quota data semantics. |\n98\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers report semantics and export integration. |\n99\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers the consumption-vs-quota view. |\n100\t\n101\tNon-edges, deliberately:\n102\t\n103\t- **No E001 → E002 edge**: the P0 reporting work does not consume the quota\n104\t  surface; keeping them parallel prevents a P1 enabler from blocking all P0\n105\t  work (priority-inversion guard).\n106\t- **No edge to/from RHAISTRAT-9990**: it is another strategy, not an epic in\n107\t  this DAG. Its schema finality is expressed as ACs (conformance gate) and\n108\t  Risks on E002/E003, per the Rule 21 \"third party resolves\" pattern plus\n109\t  tiered delivery.\n110\t- **No Investigation epic**: see Open Question Evaluation above.\n111\t\n112\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n113\t\n114\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n115\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n116\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E002 | Per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges. |\n117\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E002 (bundled) — CSV export and stable API retrieval are access modes of the same per-project report surface HLR-1 builds; a split would build the same report data surface twice and serialize presentation work behind it, so it is not separately schedulable. | Export + API stay with the report computation. |\n118\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 (quota-data enabler), E003 (admin view) | Quota side (E001) and the Dashboard comparison view (E003). |\n119\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | Documentation of report semantics and export integration. |\n120\t\n121\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n122\t\n123\t## Health Warnings\n124\t\n125\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): Affected Components has no\n126\t   per-component change descriptions or owners; Impacted Teams table,\n127\t   Dependencies table, Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and NFRs are\n128\t   absent. Epic scopes, teams, and ACs were derived from the HLRs and the\n129\t   architecture-context owning teams. Human verification of the inferred\n130\t   scopes is recommended at review.\n131\t2. **External dependency timing risk** (the strategy's open question): the\n132\t   metering data schema is owned by RHAISTRAT-9990 and is not final until\n133\t   that strategy lands. No epic is invented for it (it resolves itself);\n134\t   conformance is an AC gate on E002/E003 and the semantics risk is noted on\n135\t   E004. Timing is outside this strategy's control — a schedule risk, not an\n136\t   acceptance criterion.\n137\t3. **Architecture tension on the reporting data path** (scope trap): the\n138\t   Dashboard architecture context states the Dashboard \"owns no data plane\"\n139\t   and its interfaces are \"Kubernetes API only; no private component APIs\".\n140\t   HLR-1/HLR-2 require computing reports from non-CR metering data and\n141\t   exposing a stable API for finance tooling. The strategy does not specify\n142\t   the consumption/access surface; the decomposition keeps this at functional\n143\t   level (consume the metering delivery as provided by RHAISTRAT-9990) and\n144\t   flags the ungrounded API surface rather than inventing one.\n145\t4. **Inferred Distributed Workloads scope**: the strategy lists Distributed\n146\t   Workloads as affected but describes no change for it. HLR-3's\n147\t   per-project Kueue quota comparison is the only DW-adjacent requirement,\n148\t   and current Kueue metrics (pending/admitted workloads per queue) do not\n149\t   expose per-project GPU quota usage, so E001 scopes that exposure. If\n150\t   review determines the Dashboard can read sufficient quota data directly\n151\t   from existing Kueue CRs, E001 reduces to a validation acceptance\n152\t   criterion on E003.\n153\t5. **Inferred docs team**: no Impacted Teams table exists; E004 is assigned\n154\t   to the RHOAI Dashboard team as the primary delivering team for the\n155\t   documented capability.\n156\t6. **Priority inversions**: none found. E002 (P0) blocks no P0-lower work;\n157\t   E001/E003 (P1) do not gate any P0 epic.\n158\t\n159\t## Tiered Delivery\n160\t\n161\tExternal dependency with uncertain timing: the metering data schema owned by\n162\tRHAISTRAT-9990 (in flight). Can the strategy deliver partial value without\n163\tthe final schema? **Yes** — the metering data is already being delivered by\n164\tthe in-flight strategy, so:\n165\t\n166\t- **Tier 1 (independent work, starts now)**: E001 (fully independent of\n167\t  metering data — quota side only), E002 and E003 implemented and validated\n168\t  against the metering data as currently delivered.\n169\t- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated)**: final-schema conformance — once RHAISTRAT-9990\n170\t  lands, the reporting output is re-validated against the finalized schema\n171\t  and the documentation reflects the final report semantics. This gate is\n172\t  expressed as acceptance criteria on E002/E003 (and a semantics AC on E004),\n173\t  not as separate epics. Fallback if the final schema diverges: adapt the\n174\t  reporting consumption layer (fix-and-retry); the reporting surfaces and\n175\t  quota work are unaffected.\n176\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99932b429b3b4205","agent_id":"aef7897d48a8721f5","session_id":"bb15c9ed-6003-4c9d-b6c4-e899274a0ed5","uuid":"1b5c17ae-0bf9-4d50-bdfd-df6e179b1901","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:39:32.985Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-96c82569cca3d1ac","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
