{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b594838979a5f700","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports with CSV export and reporting API\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: -1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: -1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports with CSV export and reporting API\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the administrator-facing per-project GPU-hour consumption\n34\treporting in the Dashboard: reports of per-project GPU-hour usage over\n35\tselectable time ranges, computed from the per-project GPU-hour usage data\n36\tdelivered by the GPU usage metering work (RHAISTRAT-9990). It also delivers\n37\tthe export and retrieval access modes of the same reports — CSV export and a\n38\tstable API for finance tooling. Collection of usage data is owned by the\n39\tmetering strategy and is not re-implemented here.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Administrator report view in the Dashboard: per-project GPU-hour\n44\t  consumption over administrator-selectable time ranges.\n45\t- Report computation consumes the metering data as delivered by the GPU\n46\t  usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990); no re-implementation of usage\n47\t  collection.\n48\t- CSV export of the displayed report (same project/time-range data).\n49\t- Stable retrieval API over the same report data, suitable for finance\n50\t  tooling integration.\n51\t- Administrator-only access to the reports, export, and API.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- An administrator can view per-project GPU-hour consumption for a\n56\t  selectable time range, computed from the delivered metering data.\n57\t- The report for a given project and time range can be exported as CSV and\n58\t  opens correctly in spreadsheet tooling.\n59\t- The same report data is retrievable through a stable API usable by\n60\t  finance tooling.\n61\t- Report access (view, export, API) is restricted to platform\n62\t  administrators.\n63\t- Report computation conforms to the metering data schema as finalized by\n64\t  the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990); schema finalization\n65\t  changes are absorbed in the consumption layer and the reports re-validate\n66\t  cleanly against the finalized schema.\n67\t\n68\t## Risks / Notes\n69\t\n70\t- The metering data schema is owned by RHAISTRAT-9990 and is not final until\n71\t  that strategy lands; this epic carries that external timing risk. Reports\n72\t  are implemented and validated against the metering data as currently\n73\t  delivered and re-validated at finalization (fix-and-adapt).\n74\t- The Dashboard architecture (no data plane; Kubernetes API only) does not\n75\t  currently define a surface for non-CR time-series data or an external\n76\t  report API; the consumption path and API surface must align with what the\n77\t  metering strategy delivers. Flagged in the decomposition health warnings —\n78\t  not an acceptance criterion on this epic's deliverable.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- HLR-1 (P0) — administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption\n83\t  reports over selectable time ranges.\n84\t- HLR-2 (P1, bundled) — CSV export and stable API retrieval are access modes\n85\t  of the same report surface built for HLR-1; they share the report data\n86\t  structure and are not separately schedulable, so they are kept in this\n87\t  epic rather than split out.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99932b429b3b4205","agent_id":"aef7897d48a8721f5","session_id":"bb15c9ed-6003-4c9d-b6c4-e899274a0ed5","uuid":"e03ac753-e2fb-4766-9954-07cecd134d6d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:39:36.440Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b594838979a5f700","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
