n43\t(\"does the answer change which downstream epics exist or what they do?\"):\n44\t\n45\t- **Which epics exist**: unchanged. The reporting view, export/API, quota\n46\t  comparison view, and documentation epics exist regardless of the schema's\n47\t  final shape.\n48\t- **What they do**: unchanged at the functional level. The schema shape is a\n49\t  consumption-layer detail of the reporting implementation; resolution\n50\t  requires no technical work by these teams — the answer arrives when the\n51\t  sibling strategy lands. Failure mode is fix-and-adapt (adjust the\n52\t  consumption layer), i.e. an acceptance-criterion gate, not an\n53\t  investigation.\n54\t- The dependency is a sibling **internal strategy** that resolves itself\n55\t  (analogous to Rule 21's \"third party resolves\" case): modeled as a\n56\t  **precondition with tiered delivery** (see Tiered Delivery), with no epic\n57\t  invented for RHAISTRAT-9990 and no DAG edge to it (there is no epic to edge\n58\t  to).\n59\t\n60\tConclusion: **no Investigation epic**. The risk is carried as ACs plus\n61\tRisks/Notes on the consuming epics and as a health warning below.\n62\t\n63\t## Epic List\n64\t\n65\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n66\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n67\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E001 | Expose per-project Kueue GPU quota data for administrator consumption reporting | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n68\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 | Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports with CSV export and reporting API | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P0 |\n69\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Administrator view of current-month consumption against Kueue quota | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n70\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 | Documentation of chargeback report semantics and export integration | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | Documentation | P1 |\n71\t\n72\tPriorities: E002 carries HLR-1 (P0). E001 and E003 carry HLR-3 (P1). E004 is a\n73\t`docs-authoring` epic — exempt from priority inheritance; its priority is\n74\tderived from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 (HLR-4 is P2 in\n75\tthe HLR table, but the docs-authoring priority exception governs the epic).\n76\t\n77\t## Dependency DAG\n78\t\n79\t```mermaid\n80\tgraph TD\n81\t    E001[\"E001 — per-project Kueue GPU quota data (DW)\"] --> E003[\"E003 — consumption vs quota admin view\"]\n82\t    E002[\"E002 — consumption reports + CSV/API (Dashboard)\"] --> E003\n83\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 — report semantics & export docs\"]\n84\t    E002 --> E004\n85\t    E003 --> E004\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\tCritical path: E001 → E003 → E004 (and E002 → E003 → E004), length 3.\n89\t\n90\t## DAG Justification\n91\t\n92\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n93\t|------|------|-----------|\n94\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (build-against artifact) | The quota-comparison view's code builds against the per-project quota surface E001 exposes (an API/CR/metrics surface, not a configuration reference). |\n95\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 12/13 + shared-surface rule | The quota view displays current-month consumption, which is the report capability over a fixed time range; the edge prevents two epics building the same consumption-data surface independently. |\n96\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built, including the quota data semantics. |\n97\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers report semantics and export integration. |\n98\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers the consumption-vs-quota view. |\n99\t\n100\tNon-edges, deliberately:\n101\t\n102\t- **No E001 → E002 edge**: the P0 reporting work does not consume the quota\n103\t  surface; keeping them parallel prevents a P1 enabler from blocking all P0\n104\t  work (priority-inversion guard).\n105\t- **No edge to/from RHAISTRAT-9990**: it is another strategy, not an epic in\n106\t  this DAG. Its schema finality is expressed as ACs (conformance gate) and\n107\t  Risks on E002/E003, per the Rule 21 \"third party resolves\" pattern plus\n108\t  tiered delivery.\n109\t- **No Investigation epic**: see Open Question Evaluation above.\n110\t\n111\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n112\t\n113\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n114\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n115\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E002 | Per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges. |\n116\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E002 (bundled) — CSV export and stable API retrieval are access modes of the same per-project report surface HLR-1 builds; a split would build the same report data surface twice and serialize presentation work behind it, so it is not separately schedulable. | Export + API stay with the report computation. |\n117\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 (quota-data enabler), E003 (admin view) | Quota side (E001) and the Dashboard comparison view (E003). |\n118\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | Documentation of report semantics and export integration. |\n119\t\n120\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n121\t\n122\t## Health Warnings\n123\t\n124\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): Affected Components has no\n125\t   per-component change descriptions or owners; Impacted Teams table,\n126\t   Dependencies table, Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and NFRs are\n127\t   absent. Epic scopes, teams, and ACs were derived from the HLRs and the\n128\t   architecture-context owning teams. Human verification of the inferred\n129\t   scopes is recommended at review.\n130\t2. **External dependency timing risk** (the strategy's open question): the\n131\t   metering data schema is owned by RHAISTRAT-9990 and is not final until\n132\t   that strategy lands. No epic is invented for it (it resolves itself);\n133\t   conformance is an AC gate on E002/E003 and the semantics risk is noted on\n134\t   E004. Timing is outside this strategy's control — a schedule risk, not an\n135\t   acceptance criterion.\n136\t3. **Architecture tension on the reporting data path** (scope trap): the\n137\t   Dashboard architecture context states the Dashboard \"owns no data plane\"\n138\t   and its interfaces are \"Kubernetes API only; no private component APIs\".\n139\t   HLR-1/HLR-2 require computing reports from non-CR metering data and\n140\t   exposing a stable API for finance tooling. The strategy does not specify\n141\t   the consumption/access surface; the decomposition keeps this at functional\n142\t   level (consume the metering delivery as provided by RHAISTRAT-9990) and\n143\t   flags the ungrounded API surface rather than inventing one.\n144\t4. **Inferred Distributed Workloads scope**: the strategy lists Distributed\n145\t   Workloads as affected but describes no change for it. HLR-3's\n146\t   per-project Kueue quota comparison is the only DW-adjacent requirement,\n147\t   and current Kueue metrics (pending/admitted workloads per queue) do not\n148\t   expose per-project GPU quota usage, so E001 scopes that exposure. If\n149\t   review determines the Dashboard can read sufficient quota data directly\n150\t   from existing Kueue CRs, E001 reduces to a validation acceptance\n151\t   criterion on E003.\n152\t5. **Inferred docs team**: no Impacted Teams table exists; E004 is assigned\n153\t   to the RHOAI Dashboard team as the primary delivering team for the\n154\t   documented capability.\n155\t6. **Priority inversions**: none found. E002 (P0) blocks no P0-lower work;\n156\t   E001/E003 (P1) do not gate any P0 epic.\n157\t\n158\t## Tiered Delivery\n159\t\n160\tExternal dependency with uncertain timing: the metering data schema owned by\n161\tRHAISTRAT-9990 (in flight). Can the strategy deliver partial value without\n162\tthe final schema? **Yes** — the metering data is already being delivered by\n163\tthe in-flight strategy, so:\n164\t\n165\t- **Tier 1 (independent work, starts now)**: E001 (fully independent of\n166\t  metering data — quota side only), E002 and E003 implemented and validated\n167\t  against the metering data as currently delivered.\n168\t- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated)**: final-schema conformance — once RHAISTRAT-9990\n169\t  lands, the reporting output is re-validated against the finalized schema\n170\t  and the documentation reflects the final report semantics. This gate is\n171\t  expressed as acceptance criteria on E002/E003 (and a semantics AC on E004),\n172\t  not as separate epics. Fallback if the final schema diverges: adapt the\n173\t  reporting consumption layer (fix-and-retry); the reporting surfaces and\n174\t  quota work are unaffected.\n175\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6f76be7986fa7ed","agent_id":"a3760a6a9db45a1e7","session_id":"bb15c9ed-6003-4c9d-b6c4-e899274a0ed5","uuid":"3a87b60b-e569-42d1-8a08-c6ffcfc30df0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:43:50.751Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0a1c9f50a122119","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
