{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bde9be1b963be1cd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Expose per-project Kueue GPU quota data for administrator consumption reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Expose per-project Kueue GPU quota data for administrator consumption reporting\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a consumable, per-project view of Kueue GPU quota and\n34\tcurrent quota usage in the Distributed Workloads component, so that\n35\tadministrator-facing chargeback reporting can compare each project's GPU-hour\n36\tconsumption against its Kueue quota. Today the platform's Kueue metrics\n37\texpose pending/admitted workload counts per queue, which is not sufficient\n38\tfor per-project GPU quota comparison; this epic provides that data surface.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Expose, per project (namespace), the project's Kueue GPU quota and current\n43\t  quota usage, derived from the platform's Kueue quota model\n44\t  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue semantics).\n45\t- Choose and implement the exposure surface (metrics, custom resource, or\n46\t  API) — an implementation decision for the Distributed Workloads team; the\n47\t  strategy does not prescribe one.\n48\t- Document the exposed data contract (shape and semantics of the per-project\n49\t  quota information) for consuming teams.\n50\t- Ensure projects without a Kueue quota are represented predictably\n51\t  (reportable as no-quota) rather than omitted silently.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- For every project that has a Kueue GPU quota, the project's GPU quota and\n56\t  current quota usage are retrievable through the exposed surface.\n57\t- The exposed quota information is consistent with the platform's Kueue\n58\t  quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue semantics), verified against the\n59\t  deployed Kueue configuration.\n60\t- The data contract of the exposed surface is documented.\n61\t- Existing Kueue queueing and admission behavior is unchanged (regression\n62\t  check on the queueing path).\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-3 (P1) — enables the quota side of \"current-month consumption against\n67\t  each project's Kueue quota\" in the administrator view.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6f76be7986fa7ed","agent_id":"a3760a6a9db45a1e7","session_id":"bb15c9ed-6003-4c9d-b6c4-e899274a0ed5","uuid":"5423f4f9-f728-41b4-a443-f80921050137","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:43:55.289Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bde9be1b963be1cd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
