{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b53256969a75c3f7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E004\n3\ttitle: Documentation of chargeback report semantics and export integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E003\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 0\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 1\n19\t  open_questions: -1\n20\t  external_dependency: 0\n21\t  human_process_gates: -1\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 0\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: Medium\n26\tai_implementability_score: 1\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgated_by: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact: null\n31\t---\n32\t# Documentation of chargeback report semantics and export integration\n33\t\n34\t## Description\n35\t\n36\tThis epic delivers the administrator and finance-tooling documentation for\n37\tGPU chargeback reporting: what the reports mean (in particular what counts as\n38\ta GPU-hour and how per-project attribution works) and how to integrate with\n39\tthe report export (CSV) and retrieval API. It documents the capability as\n40\tbuilt, so it runs after the implementation work.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\tContent outline:\n45\t\n46\t- Report semantics: what counts as a GPU-hour, how per-project attribution\n47\t  is derived from the metering data, and how selectable time ranges affect\n48\t  the reported figures.\n49\t- Reading the consumption-vs-quota administrator view: what the quota\n50\t  comparison shows and how to interpret projects without a quota.\n51\t- Export integration for finance tooling: retrieving reports via the stable\n52\t  API and consuming the CSV export.\n53\t- Access prerequisites for administrators (permissions required to view\n54\t  reports).\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Documentation covers report semantics, including a clear definition of\n59\t  what counts as a GPU-hour, consistent with the semantics finalized by the\n60\t  GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990).\n61\t- Documentation covers export integration (CSV export and API retrieval) for\n62\t  finance tooling.\n63\t- Documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented reporting\n64\t  capability by the implementing team before publication.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-4 (P2) — documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a\n69\t  GPU-hour) and export integration.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88b1939eca94a553","agent_id":"a2bc11baaad4a4e6d","session_id":"bb15c9ed-6003-4c9d-b6c4-e899274a0ed5","uuid":"d4e79992-7727-44c8-a14c-d3e6bf92f6a0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:44:58.446Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b53256969a75c3f7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9018"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b667cf5ca3fb6cf3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E003\n3\ttitle: Administrator view of current-month consumption against Kueue quota\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 6\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Administrator view of current-month consumption against Kueue quota\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the Dashboard administrator view showing each project's\n36\tcurrent-month GPU-hour consumption alongside that project's Kueue GPU quota,\n37\tso administrators can see how much of each project's quota has been consumed\n38\tthis month. It consumes two existing capabilities rather than re-implementing\n39\tthem: the per-project consumption reporting delivered for chargeback\n40\treporting, and the per-project Kueue GPU quota data exposed by the\n41\tDistributed Workloads component.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Administrator view in the Dashboard listing projects with their\n46\t  current-month GPU-hour consumption and their Kueue GPU quota, presented as\n47\t  a consumption-vs-quota comparison.\n48\t- Reuse of the per-project report capability for the current-month\n49\t  consumption figures (current month is a fixed time range of the same\n50\t  report data) — no independent consumption-data retrieval.\n51\t- Reuse of the per-project quota data surface exposed by the Distributed\n52\t  Workloads component for the quota figures — no independent quota\n53\t  computation.\n54\t- Administrator-only access.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The administrator view shows, per project, current-month GPU-hour\n59\t  consumption alongside the project's Kueue GPU quota.\n60\t- Consumption figures come from the chargeback reporting capability and\n61\t  quota figures from the exposed per-project quota data; neither is\n62\t  re-implemented in this epic.\n63\t- Projects without a Kueue quota are shown as no-quota in the view, per the\n64\t  documented data contract of the exposed per-project quota surface, rather\n65\t  than silently omitted.\n66\t- View access is restricted to platform administrators.\n67\t- The view's current-month consumption figures, obtained through the\n68\t  per-project report capability, re-validate cleanly against the metering\n69\t  data schema as finalized by the GPU usage metering strategy\n70\t  (RHAISTRAT-9990); schema finalization changes are absorbed upstream in\n71\t  the report consumption layer, not re-implemented in this view.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-3 (P1) — the Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption\n76\t  against each project's Kueue quota.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88b1939eca94a553","agent_id":"a2bc11baaad4a4e6d","session_id":"bb15c9ed-6003-4c9d-b6c4-e899274a0ed5","uuid":"22937d90-2034-40ef-b13d-0e05312c0df7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:44:58.448Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b667cf5ca3fb6cf3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9018"}
